Z||000000||prodea||09-03-2001||09:40 PM||||Hi there.  I finally find a right place. I think I'm a trouble now,,, so pls. help.<BR>I own a 1987 Fiero Gt, and recently modified to 3.1 crank&fly wheel, performance cam, roller rocket arms, throw out bearings, stiffer valve springs, stage I clutch, complete rebuilt, and injector clean up for can$6000. and I think i was a rip off.<BR>I went to dyno yesterday, and result was;<BR>131.9HP@4500rpm 170ft-lbs@3600rpm.<BR>On my Fiero Owner's manual it says;<BR>140HP@5200rpm 170ft-lbs@3600rpm.<BR>Does this mean that my car with 3.1L motor has the same Torque as the stock 2.8L Fiero??<BR>I know that Dyno results are all at Tires, but how is those #s on Owners Manual? are they measured at Engine or Tires?? How are these # look like?? should't my car have more Torque & HP now with 3.1L motor???<BR>Pls. help me !! thanx !!||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||09-03-2001||09:46 PM||||Multiple by about 17% for crank HP which is what the manual gives. About 153HP. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||09-03-2001||10:28 PM||||Factory numbers are at the f/w. <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||prodea||09-03-2001||11:51 PM||||THanx for the replies!! <BR>but how do think about the cost and my car's performance regarding to the dyno result i put??  thanks !||||reg||1
