Z||000008||artherd||09-04-2001||03:02 AM||||horsepower seems low, even when you add 15% for drivetrain losses. (150bhp)<P>cost also a bit extravigant, though not hugely. New motor?  if you have a shop do it here, a 3.4 will run about $4kUSD.  <P>Profesional automotive repair is expensive.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000009||BC-GT||09-04-2001||11:44 AM||||From what I've found here in BC, 6 grand for that much work is NOT out of line, assuming that most of your parts are all new.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||lou_dias||09-04-2001||11:50 AM||||I don't know how far off that is.<BR>My rebuilt 3.4 dynoed at 150hp/203ft*lbs of torque at the wheels with a stock TB but ported heads intake and headers, K&N, roller 1.52 rocker and a CRANE compucam.  It should go up once I put in the bigger TB.  I think he forgot to get an adjustable fuel pressure regulator and set it at 44psi at idle then he should be closer to 140hp...  Also, I think driveline losses are higher in a Fiero for some reason.<BR>I still think these engines should be making more power but I think it's because of the pistons.  Everybody who's done cheap 3.1/4 conversions uses dished pistons even though the factory fiero 2.8 pistons had valve reliefs and were flat.  The only people who seem happy with their 3.4pushrod's power are the ones that use 3.4TDC pistons.  In other words, HIGH COMPRESSION.  I swear my stock (K&N + blocked off EGR) has almost as much HP (but not torque) as my 87 performace 3.4.<BR>Has to be the pistons.  Dished pistons will lower your compression ratio.  My 87 will run on 87 octane but my 88 is more peculiar and partial to 89-93 (probably due to the EGR).||||reg||1
Z||000011||prodea||09-04-2001||01:25 PM||||Thanx for replies !! Yeah i guess price isn't that much off then.... but still my car is supposed to be getting more horses.. I really need to see my mechanic and talk about this.. thanx !!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/cocoroweb/Friends/Rich.jpg">  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/cocoroweb/fiero.ram" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/cocoroweb/fiero.ram</A>  ||||reg||10
Z||000012||88formula||09-04-2001||04:41 PM||||150 Horsepower is a little low but about right for a 3.1 engine with stock heads, exhaust and intake. Roller rockers don't add much power, maybe five horsepower. <P>What camshaft do you have? Did you port out the restrictions in the stock exhaust manifold? Porting the stock exhaust manifolds yields about 8 horsepower on a 2.8-liter engine. <P>Did the dyno place monitor your air fuel ratio? Did you try different base timing settings?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||prodea||09-04-2001||05:07 PM||||Hi there! thanx again. yes I did ported the manifold! <BR>For the Dyno thing, i think they didn't monitor the Air Fuel ratio. i will ask for it next time.. you know before i do this modification I was told it's gonna get 180HP. <BR>As some of u suggested, i will look into the Fuel pressure and other factors which might be causing this lack of power. Thanx !<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid26/p8846bb17f5efe5a9d58f02727557367a/fe4080b9.jpg">  ||||reg||1
